# Olsenella intestinalis sp. nov., isolated from cow feces

Yong Guan · Zhun Li · Min-Ju Kim · Jae-Young Lee · Hanna Choe · Se Hee Park · Se Won Kang · Jiyoung Lee · Ju Huck Lee · Hyeun Bum Kim · Ju Hye Lee · Eunkyoung Kim · Mi Kyung Lee

_Archives of Microbiology_ **204**, 384 (2022). https://doi.org/10.1007/s00203-022-03017-2

## Abstract

A Gram-stain-negative, anaerobic, non-motile, rod-shaped bacterium, designated as BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\), was isolated from the feces of a cow in Andong, Republic of Korea. Polyphasic taxonomic analysis based on the 16S rRNA gene revealed strain BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) formed a lineage within the genus _Olsenella_ and was most closely related to _O. umbonate_ KCTC 15140\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) (98.2%). The complete genome sequence of strain BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) was 2,476,083 bp long with a G + C content of 66.9 mol% and contained 1835 genes and 8 contigs. The N50 value was 604,117 bp. Fifty tRNAs, six rRNAs (5S, 16S, 23S), 1778 CDSs, 2 BGCs, and 1 tmRNA were annotated. Genomic distances to the closest relative — **ANI 76.8%, AAI 67.3%, dDDH 22.2%** — were all below species-delineation thresholds. Genes for cell-wall-degrading enzymes (chitinases, \(\beta\)-1,3-glucanases, proteases) were detected. Physiological range: pH 6.0–8.0 (opt. 7.0), 0.5–1.5% NaCl (opt. 0.5%, w/v), 35–40 °C (opt. 35 °C). Predominant fatty acids: \(\mathrm{C}_{16:0}\) DMA 20.2%, \(\mathrm{C}_{16:0}\) 20.2%, \(\mathrm{C}_{18:0}\) 10.5%, \(\mathrm{C}_{18:1}\) _cis_ 9 17.0%. Polar lipids: one unidentified phospholipid, four unidentified glycolipids, three unidentified lipids. Based on phenotypic, phylogenetic, and physiological characteristics, strain BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) represents a novel species within the genus _Olsenella_ for which the name **Olsenella intestinalis sp. nov.** is proposed. Type strain BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) (= KCTC 25379\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) = GDMCC 1.3011\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\)).

**Keywords:** 16S rRNA sequence · Novel species · Polyphasic approach · Taxonomy

## 1 Introduction

The bacterial genus _Olsenella_ (family _Atopobiaceae_) was described by Dewhirst et al. (2001) with _Olsenella uli_ as type species. Kraatz et al. (2011) added phenotypic descriptions and described _Olsenella umbonata_. Nouioui et al. (2018) noted _Olsenella_ was paraphyletic; Zgheib et al. (2021) further reclassified. Lu et al. (2021) transferred _O. gallinarum_ to _Thermophilibacter_. As of late 2021, _Olsenella_ contained seven validly-published species: _O. massiliensis_, _O. phocaeensis_, _O. porci_, _O. profusa_, _O. uli_, _O. umbonate_, _O. urininfantis_. The genus is associated with bovine rumen, human/pig feces, human gingival crevice, sheep rumen, pig jejunum. Characteristic G+C content is 62–64 mol%. Strain BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\), isolated from cow feces, is proposed as a novel species.

## 2 Materials and methods

### 2.1 Isolation, preservation, cultivation

Cow feces from Andong, Republic of Korea; anaerobic pouch (GasPak\({}^{\mathrm{TM}}\) EZ), 4 °C storage. Anaerobic chamber (Coy) 7% CO\({}_{2}\)/86% N\({}_{2}\)/7% H\({}_{2}\). Serial 10-fold dilutions to \(10^{-5}\), 150 µl on TSA + 5% sheep-blood (TSAB). 35 °C, 3 days. Colonies picked → BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\). 10% skim milk −20 °C then −80 °C. Reference strains _O. umbonata_ KCTC 15140\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) and _O. profusa_ KCTC 15029\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\).

### 2.2 Phylogenetic analyses

Universal primers 27F, 518F, 805R, 1492R; 1423-bp 16S assembled in BioEdit, deposited as **OM533390**. EzBioCloud identification. Clustal W alignment; MEGA v7.0 NJ/ML/ME with 1000-bootstrap; Kimura 2-parameter distance.

### 2.3 Genomic analyses

DNA: PowerSoil® Pro Kit (Qiagen 47014). Illumina Nexa + Oxford Nanopore MinION (SQK-LSK109 / FLO-MIN106 R9.4 / MinKnow v1.15.1). Genomic correlations: ANI (EzBioCloud), dDDH (GGDC), AAI (enve-omics.ce.gatech.edu). Phylogenomic tree: TYGS (Meier-Kolthoff & Göker 2019) using GBDP + FastME 2.1.6.1 + SPR + 100 pseudo-bootstraps. Annotation: Prokka + KEGG + KEGG-Decoder + RAST.

### 2.4 Morphology / physiology / biochemistry

SEM (SPI-Dry critical-point drier + Safematic CCU-010HV gold coating). Gram stain (Difco). pH 3–9. Temperature 15–45 °C in 5 °C steps. NaCl 0.5–6%. Catalase/oxidase (Bio Mérieux). API 20 NE, API ZYM, Rapid ID 32A. Polar lipids: TLC silica gel 60 F\({}_{254}\), stained with 50% H\({}_{2}\)SO\({}_{4}\), 0.1% ninhydrin, molybdenum. Fatty acids: MIDI/HP MIS + Sherlock™ Anaerobic v6.1 on GC-210 Shimadzu.

## 3 Results and discussion

### 3.1 Phylogenetic characteristics

EzBioCloud top hits vs BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) 16S:

| Neighbor                                            | % identity |
|-----------------------------------------------------|-----------:|
| _O. umbonata_ KCTC 15140\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\)         |     98.24  |
| _O. profusa_ KCTC 15029\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\)          |     97.46  |
| _O. uli_ DSM 7084\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\)                |     96.55  |
| _Fannyhessea vaginae_ DSM 15829\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\)  |     94.86  |
| _Lancefieldella parvula_ DSM 20469\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\)|     94.07  |
| _Paratractidigestivibacter faecalis_ KCTC 15699\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\)| 93.09 |

All below 98.65% novel-species cutoff (Kim et al. 2014). NJ/ML/ME trees (Figs. 1, S1, S2) place BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) in _Olsenella_. Outgroup: _Eggerthella guodeyinii_ HF-1101\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) (MN203625).

### 3.2 Phylogenomics and genomic analyses

TYGS tree (Fig. 2) shows BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) in a distinct species branch. dDDH < 70% cutoff; ANI ≤ 76.8% < 95–96% species threshold; AAI (BGYT1 vs _O. umbonata_) = 67.3%; dDDH = 22.2%. Genome (paper body text): 1835 genes, 8 contigs, **2,453,694 bp**, N50 = 604,117 bp, 50 tRNAs, 6 rRNAs (5S/16S/23S), 1 tmRNA, 1778 CDSs, 2 BGCs, G+C = 66.9%. Table 1 collects AAI/ANI/dDDH.

_Note: abstract states 2,476,083 bp, but body text and both NCBI assemblies (GCF_023276655.1, GCA_023276655.1) report 2,453,694 bp in 2 contigs. Discrepancy is internal to the paper._

Functional annotation (COG): strong signals in cell wall/membrane/envelope biogenesis, translation, carbohydrate/nucleotide/lipid/inorganic-ion transport & metabolism, transcription, signal transduction, defense mechanisms (Fig. 3). Detected: chitinases, β-1,3-glucanases, proteases.

### 3.3 Morphological, physiological and biochemical features

Colonies TSAB / 35 °C / 2d: circular, convex, smooth, entire. Anaerobic, non-motile, oxidase\({}^-\), catalase\({}^-\). Rods 1.5–3.1 × 0.2–0.3 μm (Fig. S3). Growth: pH 6.0–8.0, 35–40 °C, 0.5–1.5% NaCl (opt. 0.5%). Urease\({}^+\) (API 20A). Positive: alkaline phosphatase, arginine, β-glucosidase, arginine dihydrolase (Table S2). Fatty acids (>10%): C\({}_{16:0}\) 20.2%, C\({}_{16:0}\) DMA 20.2%, C\({}_{18:0}\) 10.5%, C\({}_{18:1}\) _cis_ 9 17.0%. Extra vs. _O. umbonata_: higher C\({}_{16:0}\) and presence of C\({}_{18:2}\) _cis_ 9,12 (Table S3). Polar lipids: 1 phospholipid + 4 glycolipids + 3 lipids (all unidentified).

### 3.4 Taxonomic conclusion

Genomic (ANI 76.8% / AAI 67.3% / dDDH 22.2%) and phenotypic evidence supports _Olsenella intestinalis_ sp. nov.

## 4 Description of _Olsenella intestinalis_ sp. nov.

_O. intestinalis_ (in.tes.ti.na'lis. L. fem. adj., "pertaining to the intestine"). Anaerobic, Gram-stain-negative, non-motile rods, 1.5–3.1 × 0.2–0.3 μm. Colonies circular/convex/smooth/entire on TSAB (35 °C, 2 d). Growth pH 6.0–8.0 (opt. 7.0), 35–40 °C (opt. 35 °C), 0.5–1.5% NaCl (opt. 0.5%). Oxidase\({}^-\), catalase\({}^-\). Predominant FA: C\({}_{16:0}\) DMA, C\({}_{16:0}\), C\({}_{18:0}\), C\({}_{18:1}\) _cis_ 9. Type strain **BGYT1\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) (= KCTC 25379\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\) = GDMCC 1.3011\({}^{\mathrm{T}}\))** from cow feces (Andong, Korea). Genome G+C = 66.9%. Accessions: **OM533390** (16S), **JALGRK000000000** (whole genome).

